×5 table; write a rule from 2,5,8,11. Prefer a named rule over a single guess.\n\nTRY FIRST\nGive the rule for 100, 90, 80, 70 and the next term.\n\nFEEDBACK\nSubtract 10; next 60.","explain":"Pattern fluency practises stating rules, extending sequences and reading input–output tables accurately.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Two different rules that fit only the first three terms are not secure until checked further. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Pattern fluency practice.","caption":"Verify rule further along.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Fluency</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">continue; table; rule</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Check</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">extra terms</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"t